      <h1 id="stage-22-software-domains" class="group scroll-mt-20">Stage 22: Software domains<a href="#stage-22-software-domains" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Document the <code>mod-script-pipe</code> interface with elements from DITA's software and programming domains. Create a scripting reference for command syntax, parameters, messages, and platform-specific pipe locations.</p>
      <p>Create a task that references <code>samples/export-mp3.py</code> through <code>&lt;coderef&gt;</code>. Mark up a terminal session with <code>&lt;screen&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;userinput&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;systemoutput&gt;</code>.</p>
      <p><strong>Optional module.</strong> See <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/learning-path">Choose a learning path</a> for the starting checkpoint and the next core lesson.</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> about 35 minutes. <strong>You need:</strong> stage 21 complete.</p>
      <p>Recorded diagnostic examples below come from earlier runs. File counts, paths, and stage numbers can differ. Run the gate for your current checkout.</p>
      <h2 id="step-1-the-scripting-reference" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 1: The scripting reference<a href="#step-1-the-scripting-reference" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><strong><code>topics/scripting-reference.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN\" \"reference.dtd\">\n\n\u003creference id=\"scripting-reference\">\n  \u003ctitle>Scripting commands\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>The scripting commands most useful for batch work, their parameters and the responses they return.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003cprolog>\n    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n    \u003ccritdates>\n      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-03-01\"/>\n    \u003c/critdates>\n    \u003cmetadata>\n      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"expert\"/>\n      \u003ccategory>reference\u003c/category>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>scripting\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>mod-script-pipe\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>automation\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003cindexterm>scripting\u003cindexterm>commands\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/metadata>\n  \u003c/prolog>\n  \u003crefbody>\n    \u003csection>\n      \u003ctitle>Syntax\u003c/title>\n      \u003cp>A scripting command is a command name, a colon, and zero or more \u003cvarname>Name\u003c/varname>=\u003cvarname>Value\u003c/varname> parameters.\n      \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> replies with the command's output followed by a status line.\u003c/p>\n      \u003csyntaxdiagram>\n        \u003ctitle>Scripting command\u003c/title>\n        \u003cgroupseq>\n          \u003ckwd>CommandName\u003c/kwd>\n          \u003cdelim>:\u003c/delim>\n          \u003cgroupseq importance=\"optional\">\n            \u003crepsep/>\n            \u003cvar>Name\u003c/var>\n            \u003cdelim>=\u003c/delim>\n            \u003cvar>Value\u003c/var>\n          \u003c/groupseq>\n        \u003c/groupseq>\n      \u003c/syntaxdiagram>\n      \u003cp>A synopsis in one line: \u003csynph>\u003ckwd>Export2\u003c/kwd>\u003cdelim>:\u003c/delim> \u003cvar>Filename\u003c/var>=\u003cvar>path\u003c/var> \u003cvar>NumChannels\u003c/var>=\u003cvar>1|2\u003c/var>\u003c/synph>.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/section>\n    \u003crefsyn>\n      \u003ctitle>Commands\u003c/title>\n      \u003cparml>\n        \u003cplentry>\n          \u003cpt>\n            \u003ccmdname>SelectAll:\u003c/cmdname>\n          \u003c/pt>\n          \u003cpd>Selects every track from start to end. No parameters.\u003c/pd>\n        \u003c/plentry>\n        \u003cplentry>\n          \u003cpt>\u003ccmdname>Normalize:\u003c/cmdname> \u003cparmname>PeakLevel\u003c/parmname>=\u003cvarname>dB\u003c/varname>\u003c/pt>\n          \u003cpd>Normalizes the selection so its peak sits at \u003cvarname>dB\u003c/varname>, typically \u003ccodeph>-1\u003c/codeph>.\u003c/pd>\n        \u003c/plentry>\n        \u003cplentry>\n          \u003cpt>\u003ccmdname>Export2:\u003c/cmdname> \u003cparmname>Filename\u003c/parmname>=\u003cvarname>path\u003c/varname> \u003cparmname>NumChannels\u003c/parmname>=\u003cvarname>n\u003c/varname>\u003c/pt>\n          \u003cpd>Exports the selection to \u003cvarname>path\u003c/varname>; the extension selects the format.\n          \u003coption>NumChannels=1\u003c/option> forces mono.\u003c/pd>\n        \u003c/plentry>\n        \u003cplentry>\n          \u003cpt>\u003ccmdname>GetInfo:\u003c/cmdname> \u003cparmname>Type\u003c/parmname>=\u003cvarname>Commands|Tracks|Clips\u003c/varname>\u003c/pt>\n          \u003cpd>Returns a JSON description of the requested objects.\u003c/pd>\n        \u003c/plentry>\n      \u003c/parml>\n    \u003c/refsyn>\n    \u003csection>\n      \u003ctitle>Responses\u003c/title>\n      \u003cp>Every reply ends with a status line.\n      Success looks like \u003cmsgph>BatchCommand finished: OK\u003c/msgph>; a failure names the command:\u003c/p>\n      \u003cmsgblock>Export2: Filename=episode.mp3 NumChannels=1\nBatchCommand finished: Failed!\u003c/msgblock>\n      \u003cp>The \u003capiname>send\u003c/apiname> function in the sample script (\u003cxref href=\"../samples/export-mp3.py\" scope=\"external\" format=\"py\">export-mp3.py\u003c/xref>) returns the whole reply; check it for \u003cmsgnum>Failed!\u003c/msgnum> before sending the next command.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/section>\n    \u003cproperties>\n      \u003cprophead>\n        \u003cproptypehd>Platform\u003c/proptypehd>\n        \u003cpropvaluehd>Pipe location\u003c/propvaluehd>\n        \u003cpropdeschd>Notes\u003c/propdeschd>\n      \u003c/prophead>\n      \u003cproperty platform=\"linux mac\">\n        \u003cproptype>Linux, macOS\u003c/proptype>\n        \u003cpropvalue>\n          \u003cfilepath>/tmp/audacity_script_pipe.to.\u003cvarname>uid\u003c/varname>\u003c/filepath>\n        \u003c/propvalue>\n        \u003cpropdesc>A named pipe per user id; open it for writing.\u003c/propdesc>\n      \u003c/property>\n      \u003cproperty platform=\"windows\">\n        \u003cproptype>Windows\u003c/proptype>\n        \u003cpropvalue>\n          \u003cfilepath>\\\\.\\pipe\\ToSrvPipe\u003c/filepath>\n        \u003c/propvalue>\n        \u003cpropdesc>A Windows named pipe; open it in text mode.\u003c/propdesc>\n      \u003c/property>\n    \u003c/properties>\n  \u003c/refbody>\n\u003c/reference>"} lang="xml" title="topics/scripting-reference.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the syntax diagram</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;syntaxdiagram&gt;</code> is a block that describes syntax as a tree of groups. <code>&lt;groupseq&gt;</code> is a sequence; its children are <code>&lt;kwd&gt;</code> for a literal keyword, <code>&lt;delim&gt;</code> for a delimiter, <code>&lt;var&gt;</code> for something the reader supplies. The outer sequence is <em>CommandName</em> <code>:</code> then an optional inner sequence, <code>importance="optional"</code>, of <em>Name</em> <code>=</code> <em>Value</em>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;repsep&gt;</code> in the inner sequence is the separator between repetitions of that group. It is empty here because the separator is a space, and the project's formatter trims whitespace-only text. It comes <em>first</em> inside the <code>&lt;groupseq&gt;</code> it applies to, before the keywords and variables: the content model of a group is a title, then an optional <code>&lt;repsep&gt;</code>, then the items. The demo at the end puts it in the wrong place.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;synph&gt;</code> is the inline form: a syntax phrase with the same <code>&lt;kwd&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;delim&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;var&gt;</code> children, for a one-line synopsis in running text.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the parameter list</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;refsyn&gt;</code> is the reference section for syntax; a <code>&lt;reference&gt;</code> body may hold it beside plain <code>&lt;section&gt;</code>s.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;parml&gt;</code> is a definition list for parameters: each <code>&lt;plentry&gt;</code> has a <code>&lt;pt&gt;</code> (the term) and a <code>&lt;pd&gt;</code> (its description). Inside them, <code>&lt;cmdname&gt;</code> is the command, <code>&lt;parmname&gt;</code> a named parameter, <code>&lt;varname&gt;</code> a value the reader supplies, <code>&lt;option&gt;</code> a switch that selects a behavior, <code>&lt;codeph&gt;</code> a literal value.</li>
      <li>Everything a reader types or reads on a screen gets the element that says what it is, and a stylesheet can render <code>&lt;cmdname&gt;</code> in bold and <code>&lt;varname&gt;</code> in italic without you deciding it here.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the messages</strong> <code>&lt;msgph&gt;</code> is a message quoted inline; <code>&lt;msgblock&gt;</code> is a message as a block, whitespace preserved like <code>&lt;codeblock&gt;</code>; <code>&lt;msgnum&gt;</code> is the message's identifier, here the status word <code>Failed!</code>. <code>&lt;apiname&gt;</code> is the name of a function, class or method in an API.
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the properties table</strong> <code>&lt;properties&gt;</code> is a reference table with three fixed columns: <code>&lt;proptype&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;propvalue&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;propdesc&gt;</code>, with an optional <code>&lt;prophead&gt;</code> naming them. Each <code>&lt;property&gt;</code> row carries a <code>platform</code> attribute, so the Windows builds from stage 14 show the Windows pipe and the Mac and Linux builds the other. <code>&lt;filepath&gt;</code> with a <code>&lt;varname&gt;</code> inside it names the pipe with the user id as a variable.
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-the-task-and-the-sample" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: The task and the sample<a href="#step-2-the-task-and-the-sample" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><strong><code>samples/export-mp3.py</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Export the open Audacity project as MP3 through mod-script-pipe.\"\"\"\nimport sys\n\nTO_PIPE = \"/tmp/audacity_script_pipe.to.\" + str(1000)\nFROM_PIPE = \"/tmp/audacity_script_pipe.from.\" + str(1000)\n\ndef send(command: str) -> str:\n    with open(TO_PIPE, \"w\") as to_pipe:\n        to_pipe.write(command + \"\\n\")\n    with open(FROM_PIPE) as from_pipe:\n        return from_pipe.read()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    target = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"episode.mp3\"\n    print(send(\"SelectAll:\"))\n    print(send(\"Normalize: PeakLevel=-1\"))\n    print(send(f\"Export2: Filename={target} NumChannels=1\"))"} lang="text" title="samples/export-mp3.py" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><strong><code>topics/exporting-from-a-script.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n\u003ctask id=\"exporting-from-a-script\">\n  \u003ctitle>Exporting from a script\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>Enable mod-script-pipe, then normalize and export the open project from a Python script.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003cprolog>\n    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n    \u003ccritdates>\n      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-03-01\"/>\n    \u003c/critdates>\n    \u003cmetadata>\n      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"expert\"/>\n      \u003ccategory>automation\u003c/category>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>scripting\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>Python\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>export\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003cindexterm>scripting\u003cindexterm>from Python\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/metadata>\n  \u003c/prolog>\n  \u003ctaskbody>\n    \u003cprereq>\n      \u003cp>Python 3 is installed, and a project is open in \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/prereq>\n    \u003csteps>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Choose \u003cmenucascade>\u003cuicontrol>Edit\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Preferences\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Modules\u003c/uicontrol>\u003c/menucascade>, set \u003cuicontrol>mod-script-pipe\u003c/uicontrol> to \u003cuicontrol>Enabled\u003c/uicontrol>, and restart \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>.\u003c/cmd>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Save the sample script as \u003cfilepath>export-mp3.py\u003c/filepath>.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cinfo>\n          \u003ccodeblock outputclass=\"language-python\">\u003ccoderef href=\"../samples/export-mp3.py\"/>\u003c/codeblock>\n        \u003c/info>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Run it, naming the output file.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cinfo>\n          \u003cscreen>\u003cuserinput>python3 export-mp3.py episode.mp3\u003c/userinput>\n\u003csystemoutput>BatchCommand finished: OK\nBatchCommand finished: OK\nBatchCommand finished: OK\u003c/systemoutput>\u003c/screen>\n        \u003c/info>\n        \u003csteptroubleshooting>\n          \u003cp>If the script hangs on the first command, the pipe does not exist: \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> is not running or the module is not enabled.\n          On Linux, \u003ccmdname>ls\u003c/cmdname> \u003cfilepath>/tmp/audacity_script_pipe.*\u003c/filepath> shows whether the pipes are there.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/steptroubleshooting>\n      \u003c/step>\n    \u003c/steps>\n    \u003cresult>\n      \u003cp>The project is normalized to -1 dB and exported as mono MP3.\n      Change \u003cparmname>NumChannels\u003c/parmname> to \u003ccodeph>2\u003c/codeph> for stereo.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/result>\n  \u003c/taskbody>\n  \u003crelated-links>\n    \u003clink href=\"scripting-reference.dita\"/>\n  \u003c/related-links>\n\u003c/task>"} lang="xml" title="topics/exporting-from-a-script.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the coderef</strong> <code>&lt;codeblock outputclass="language-python"&gt;&lt;coderef href="../samples/export-mp3.py"/&gt;&lt;/codeblock&gt;</code> is the whole listing. <code>&lt;coderef&gt;</code> is an empty element that, at build time, is replaced by the text of the file it points at, relative to the topic. The script lives once, in <code>samples/</code>, where it can be run and tested; the topic never goes stale against it. <code>outputclass</code> on the <code>&lt;codeblock&gt;</code> becomes a class on the <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> in the HTML5 output, <code>language-python</code>, the convention that syntax highlighters such as highlight.js and Prism read. In the gate's build of the full guide the listing is in place:
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003cpre class=\"pre codeblock language-python\">\u003ccode>#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Export the open Audacity project as MP3 through mod-script-pipe.\"\"\"\nimport sys\n\nTO_PIPE = \"/tmp/audacity_script_pipe.to.\" + str(1000)\nFROM_PIPE = \"/tmp/audacity_script_pipe.from.\" + str(1000)\n\ndef send(command: str) -&gt; str:\n    with open(TO_PIPE, \"w\") as to_pipe:\n        to_pipe.write(command + \"\\n\")\n    with open(FROM_PIPE) as from_pipe:\n        return from_pipe.read()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    target = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) &gt; 1 else \"episode.mp3\"\n    print(send(\"SelectAll:\"))\n    print(send(\"Normalize: PeakLevel=-1\"))\n    print(send(f\"Export2: Filename={target} NumChannels=1\"))\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>"} lang="plaintext" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the screen</strong> <code>&lt;screen&gt;</code> is a block for what a terminal shows, whitespace preserved. Inside it, <code>&lt;userinput&gt;</code> is what the reader typed and <code>&lt;systemoutput&gt;</code> what came back, so a stylesheet can tell them apart. The <code>&lt;steptroubleshooting&gt;</code> from stage 06 covers the one way the step fails, with <code>&lt;cmdname&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;filepath&gt;</code> for the check.
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit the maps</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/audacity-guide.ditamap\n+++ b/audacity-guide.ditamap\n@@ -61,6 +61,10 @@\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita\" keys=\"podcast-workflow\"/>\n   \u003c/topichead>\n \n+  \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Automation\">\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/exporting-from-a-script.dita\"/>\n+  \u003c/topichead>\n+\n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Reference\" id=\"reference\">\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" keys=\"formats\" locktitle=\"yes\">\n       \u003ctopicmeta>\n@@ -69,6 +73,7 @@\n     \u003c/topicref>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effects-reference.dita\" keys=\"effects\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effect-presets.dita\"/>\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/scripting-reference.dita\" keys=\"scripting\"/>\n   \u003c/topichead>\n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Glossary\">\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/glossary/audio-units.dita\"/>"} lang="diff" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/podcaster-guide.ditamap\n+++ b/podcaster-guide.ditamap\n@@ -36,6 +36,8 @@\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" keys=\"formats\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effects-reference.dita\" keys=\"effects\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effect-presets.dita\"/>\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/scripting-reference.dita\" keys=\"scripting\"/>\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/exporting-from-a-script.dita\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/glossary/audio-units.dita\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/glossary/g-compression.dita\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/glossary/g-normalization.dita\"/>"} lang="diff" title="podcaster-guide.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/audacity-book.ditamap\n+++ b/audacity-book.ditamap\n@@ -69,6 +69,9 @@\n   \u003cappendix href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" keys=\"formats\"/>\n   \u003cappendix href=\"topics/effects-reference.dita\" keys=\"effects\"/>\n   \u003cappendix href=\"topics/effect-presets.dita\"/>\n+  \u003cappendix href=\"topics/scripting-reference.dita\">\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/exporting-from-a-script.dita\"/>\n+  \u003c/appendix>\n \n   \u003cbackmatter>\n     \u003cbooklists>"} lang="diff" title="audacity-book.ditamap" />
      <p>The full guide gets an <em>Automation</em> head for the task and the reference under <em>Reference</em> with the key <code>scripting</code>; the podcaster guide takes both under its <em>Reference</em>; in the book the reference is a fourth appendix with the task as its section. The beginner guide does not get them.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita</code></strong>
